From cf2645f820a3df89fd6b8f1e5f16de558d213e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:16:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8173: add the frequency hopping
 controller

MT8173 has an FHCTL block at 0x10209e00 and both the binding
(mediatek,mt8173-fhctl, already listed in
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt8186-fhctl.yaml) and the
driver support for it already exist -- clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c has carried
a pllfhs[] table naming every hoppable PLL, including FH(CLK_APMIXED_MMPLL,
FH_MMPLL, 0x9c), since it was written. Only the DT node was missing, so
fhctl_parse_dt() never found anything, every PLL registered with plain
mtk_pll_ops, and the hopping path was dead code.

The block is not board specific, and MediaTek's own MT8173 kernel says so
by putting it in the SoC dtsi rather than in a board file, with the same
compatible and the same base address this patch uses:

	fhctl: fhctl@10209e00 {
		compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-fhctl";
		reg = <0 0x10209e00 0 0x100>;
	};

Its register header lays FHCTL0..FHCTL10 out at 0x38, 0x4c, 0x60, 0x74,
0x88, 0x9c, 0xb0, 0xc4, 0xd8, 0xec and 0x100, which are the same offsets
the in-tree pllfhs[] table already uses.

Two details differ from that node deliberately. The size is 0x200 rather
than 0x100 because FHCTL10's last register, MON, is at offset 0x110, so
0x100 does not cover FHCTL9 or FHCTL10 -- the vendor header labels those
two "mt8173 FHCTL B" -- and of_iomap() only hides that by mapping a whole
page. mt8186 uses 0x200 for the same reason. And the node carries a clocks
property, which the vendor's does not, because fhctl_parse_dt() takes the
list of PLLs to place under hopping control from it.

The reg range falls inside apmixedsys, which already has a sub-block
described this way in this file: hdmi-phy@10209100. Both are mapped with
of_iomap(), which does not claim the region exclusively.

Without the node, clk_set_rate() on MMPLL silently does nothing.
mtk_pll_set_rate() writes a freshly computed pcw into MMPLL CON1, but the
hardware only accepts a CON1 pcw that the frequency hopping engine has
actually ramped the PLL to: a direct write of an arbitrary pcw to CON1 is
silently dropped, both from the kernel and from /dev/mem, while a write of
the value that FHCTL's MON register currently holds is accepted. So
clk_set_rate() returns 0, mtk_pll_recalc_rate() reads back the old value,
and the caller is told nothing went wrong.

With this node MMPLL registers with mtk_pllfh_ops instead, and
hopping_hw_flow() does what the vendor's mt_gpufreq/mt_freqhopping does:
sync CON1 into the FHCTL DDS, take the PLL under hopping control, request
the new DDS, poll MON, write the achieved value back into CON1 and release
control. The rate then takes effect and persists after control returns to
CON1.

All of this was found and measured on an Amazon Fire HD 10 (2017), which is
the only MT8173 board I have. There the GPU was pinned at its bootloader
rate of 455 MHz with no way to change it, and with this node it moves:
glmark2 build reports 68 fps at 253 MHz, 87 at 455 and 91 at 598.

I cannot test the other in-tree MT8173 boards -- mt8173-evb and the
elm/hana Chromebooks -- so while the evidence above is that the block is
present on every MT8173, I cannot confirm that enabling it is sane on all
of them, and review or testing from someone with that hardware would be
welcome. Two things should limit the effect. Nothing in mainline sets
MMPLL's rate today, so until something retunes it this only changes which
ops MMPLL is registered with. And MMPLL is a selectable parent of four
muxes -- mfg_sel, vdec_sel (via mmpll_d2), msdc50_0_sel and mem_mfg_in_sel
-- of which only mfg_sel is parented to it on this board; a board that
routes any of the other three through MMPLL would see those clocks move
with it.

Only MMPLL is listed, because nothing in mainline asks to retune the other
hoppable PLLs and MMPLL is the one that is actually broken. SSC is left off
(mediatek,hopping-ssc-percent 0) to keep this a pure fix.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
index 169ba4fd1..9faeb01a2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
@@ -618,6 +618,13 @@ apmixedsys: clock-controller@10209000 {
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		fhctl: clock-controller@10209e00 {
+			compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-fhctl";
+			reg = <0 0x10209e00 0 0x200>;
+			clocks = <&apmixedsys CLK_APMIXED_MMPLL>;
+			mediatek,hopping-ssc-percent = <0>;
+		};
+
 		hdmi_phy: hdmi-phy@10209100 {
 			compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-hdmi-phy";
 			reg = <0 0x10209100 0 0x24>;
